  id: AR-2
  name: Modelo de representación / Representation Model
  position: refinement pass 2 complete; final review / closure assessment pending

invariants:
  - KOS-Lab authority preserved
  - KOS-Comm autonomy preserved
  - Binding = bilateral seam
  - KCA = neutral target
  - KCP = small and replaceable
  - KSCL = experimental/open decomposition
  - receipt != canonical import
  - communication != authority
  - representation != represented object
  - representation != authority
  - reconstruction != authorization
  - promotion = evidence + governance

working_documents:
  - docs/kos-comn/architecture/AR-1-CLOSURE.es.md
  - docs/kos-comn/architecture/AR-1-CLOSURE.en.md
  - docs/kos-comn/architecture/AR-2-REPRESENTATION-MODEL.es.md
  - docs/kos-comn/architecture/AR-2-REPRESENTATION-MODEL.en.md
  - docs/kos-comn/architecture/AR-2-REPRESENTATION-VALIDATION.es.md
  - docs/kos-comn/architecture/AR-2-REPRESENTATION-VALIDATION.en.md
  - docs/kos-comn/architecture/AR-2-REPRESENTATION-REFINEMENT.es.md
  - docs/kos-comn/architecture/AR-2-REPRESENTATION-REFINEMENT.en.md

closure_candidate:
  formula: MINIMAL_SEMANTIC_CORE + DECLARED_SEMANTIC_CAPABILITIES + OPTIONAL_EXTENSIBLE_CLASSIFICATION
  mandatory_core:
    - subject
    - semantic_context
    - capabilities
    - content
  conditional_core:
    - representation_identity
    - provenance
    - classification
  capability_criticality:
    - REQUIRED_FOR_INTERPRETATION
    - REQUIRED_FOR_DECLARED_PROPERTY
    - OPTIONAL
    - INFORMATIONAL
  interpretation_states:
    - FULL
    - DEGRADED
    - UNINTERPRETABLE

refined_findings:
  - representation_identity is conditional, not universally mandatory
  - no universal global subject identifier is required
  - unknown capability is not automatically safe to ignore
  - degradation must be explicit and conservative
  - unsupported property dependency downgrades property confidence/status
  - domain extensions may extend but not silently override core semantics
  - composition cannot elevate guarantees without justified composition rules
  - semantic criticality remains separate from protocol negotiation
  - Claim, Evidence, Verification and Guarantee are distinct

next_action:
  id: AR-2-FINAL-REVIEW
  description_es: Ejecutar revisión adversarial final y evaluación de cierre de AR-2.
  description_en: Perform final adversarial review and AR-2 closure assessment.
  decision_target: CLOSE_AR_2_OR_REWORK

adversarial_cases:
  - unknown critical capability
  - composition with degraded component
  - ephemeral representation without identity
  - subject without global identifier
  - undisclosed provenance
  - guarantee dependent on unsupported capability
  - conflicting domain extension

reentry_rule:
  - verify actual Git HEAD before development
  - reconcile CURRENT.kscl against later commits/documents
  - do not infer authority from this record

assertions:
  - CURRENT.kscl is mutable continuity state
  - checkpoint is historical snapshot
  - KSCL continuity != architectural authority
  - KSCL reconstruction != proof
